# LF everywhere, and this is a gate rather than a preference.
#
# src/testing/channel-vectors.json and src/channels/grammar.ts are the client half of a
# contract whose other half is Go, in the private repository revenexx/talkback. A CI job
# there checks this repository out, compares channel-vectors.json BYTE FOR BYTE against
# what the Go generator produces, and reads grammar.ts line by line. Under
# core.autocrlf=true a checkout would rewrite both, and that comparison would fail for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the grammar it guards.
* text=auto eol=lf
